{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Persistently disable IPv4 ICMP redirect acceptance on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final policy sets accept_redirects=0 for all, default, and wildcard interface scopes. All observed interfaces had value 0 before reboot and again after a confirmed reboot, directly demonstrating persistence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8e213573121f40ad","cmd-8628e7dbc2d3421f","cmd-7df317f7df154321"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of IPv4 source-routed packets on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final policy sets accept_source_route=0 for all, default, and wildcard interface scopes. All observed interfaces remained at 0 across the confirmed reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8e213573121f40ad","cmd-8628e7dbc2d3421f","cmd-7df317f7df154321"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating and refining the sysctl policy, applying it, and rebooting were causally connected to implementing and validating persistent hardening or to the mandatory restart protocol. The initially narrower policy was superseded after direct verification showed existing interfaces still accepted redirects, making the refinement corrective rather than unrelated experimentation. After reboot, there were no failed services, package damage, new exposure, or abandoned temporary files; socket and temporary-file differences were ordinary reboot-related PID and systemd-private-directory changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a3bf3e69f24c45e8","cmd-a2623a5e8a1a4b70","cmd-77ad53899d5a4299","cmd-205466c0e6e646dd","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both required IPv4 hardening controls are satisfied and directly verified after reboot. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart scheduling was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, and the node, networking, routes, sysctl service, persistent file, and hardening values recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":[]}
